  },
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "What is moderation ( (适度) )? {Basically} , it means eating only as much food as your body needs.You should feel {satisfied} at the end of a {meal} , but not too full.For many of us, moderation means eating {less} than we do now.But it doesn't mean saying {goodbye} to the foods you loveIt's tempting to grab delicious foods like {ice-cream} , {chocolate} , and {bacon} , so consider the following tips to control your portion ( (食物的一份) ) sizes and make mindful choices.",
      "cn": "什么是适度饮食？ 从根本上说 ，它意味着只吃身体所需的食物量。一 餐 结束后，你应该感到 满足 ，但又不会觉得吃得过饱。对我们许多人来说，适度饮食意味着要比现在吃得 更少 。但这并不意味着你要 告别 你所喜爱的食物。像 冰激凌 、 巧克力 和 培根 这类美味的食物总是很诱人，所以不妨参考以下这些建议，以控制你的食物分量，并做出慎重的选择。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Take your timeIt's important to slow down and think about food as something {nutritious} rather than just something to eat in between meetingsDon't {swallow} a meal on the way to work.It actually takes a few minutes for your {brain} to tell your body that it has had enough food, so eat slowly and {cease} to eat before you feel full.",
      "cn": "细嚼慢咽。放慢速度，把食物视为 营养 品，而不仅仅是会议间隙吃下的东西，这一点很重要。不要在上班途中狼 吞 虎咽地吃饭。实际上， 大脑 需要几分钟的时间来告诉身体它已经吃饱了，所以要慢慢吃，并在感到饱之前就 停止 进食。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "Include a variety of foods in your meals.For instance, adding {tofu} , {beans} , and {eggs} to your diet can provide essential protein without {excessive} calories.Vegetables like {tomatoes} , {onions} , and even {garlic} can enhance flavor while keeping dishes light.Cooking methods also matter.Instead of {frying} , try to {boil} or steam your food to reduce fat intake ( (摄取量) ).",
      "cn": "饮食中应包含各种食物。例如，在饮食中加入 豆腐 、 豆类 和 鸡蛋 ，既能获取必需的蛋白质，又不会摄入 过多 热量。 番茄 、 洋葱 ，甚至 大蒜 等蔬菜可以在保持菜肴清淡的同时增添风味。烹饪方法也很重要。不妨尝试 煮 或蒸食物来替代 煎炸 ，以减少脂肪的摄入。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "Eat with others {whenever} possible.Eating alone, especially in front of the {TV} or {computer} , often leads to mindless {overeating} .And be {careful} about the foods you keep at handIt's more {challenging} to eat in moderation if you have {unhealthy} snacks at the {ready} , like cookies.Instead, {surround} yourself with healthy choices.",
      "cn": "尽 可能与他人一起用餐。独自吃饭， 尤其 是在 电视 或 电脑 前，往往会导致无意识的 暴饮暴食 。还要 注意 身边存放的食物。如果身边 备 有 不健康的 零食，比如曲奇，那么适度进食就更 有挑战性 了。相反，让自己 置身 于健康的选择之中。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "Be aware of the hidden calories in foods.Items like {butter} , {cream} , and {salty} snacks can add extra fat and sodium ( (钠) ) to your meals.When dining out at a {barbecue} or enjoying a {steak} , be mindful of the portion sizes.When it comes to snacks, instead of reaching for {candy} or {sausage} , try healthier options like fresh {watermelon} or a squeeze of {lemon} in your water.",
      "cn": "注意食物中的隐藏热量。 黄油 、 奶油 和 咸味 零食等食物会给你的餐食增加额外的脂肪和钠。外出享用 烧烤 或 牛排 时，要注意分量。说到零食，与其去吃 糖果 或 香肠 ，不如尝试新鲜的 西瓜 或在水中挤点 柠檬汁 等更健康的选择。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "Control emotional {eating} .We don't always eat just to {satisfy hunger} .Many of us also turn to food to deal with {unpleasant emotions} such as {sadness} , {loneliness} , or {boredom} .But by learning healthier ways to manage emotions, you can {regain} control over the food you eat and your feelings.",
      "cn": "控制情绪化 进食 。我们吃东西并不总是为了 满足饥饿感 。我们许多人还会通过食物来应对 悲伤 、 孤独 或 无聊 等 不愉快的情绪 。但是，通过学习更健康的情绪管理方法，你可以 重新 掌控自己的饮食和情绪。"
    },
    {
      "num": "07",
      "en": "Eat properly throughout the day.A healthy {breakfast} can start your metabolism ( (新陈代谢) ), while eating small, healthy meals keeps your energy up all day.Avoid eating late at night.Try to eat dinner earlier and go without food for {fourteen} to {sixteen} hours until breakfast the next morning.Studies suggest that eating only when you're most {active} and giving your {digestive} system a long break each day may help to {regulate} weight.",
      "cn": "全天合理饮食。一顿健康的 早餐 可以启动你的新陈代谢，而少量健康的餐食能让你全天精力充沛。避免深夜进食。尽量早点吃晚餐，并坚持 14 到 16 个小时不吃东西，直到次日早餐。研究表明，只在最 活跃 的时候进食，每天给 消化 系统较长时间的休息，可能有助于 调节 体重。"
    }
  ],
